# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WEBSITE ENVIRONMENT
#
# 1. Copy this file and rename the copy to:  .env
# 2. Fill in the values.
# 3. Never put the .env file on GitHub — it is already in .gitignore.
#
# Anything prefixed VITE_ is compiled into the JavaScript the browser
# downloads, so treat every value here as PUBLIC. Nothing secret belongs in
# this file — secrets live in backend/.env, which is never sent to a browser.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Where the API lives ---------------------------------------------------
# Leave as-is for local development. In Vercel set this in Project Settings →
# Environment Variables to the Hostinger-hosted API's address, for example
# https://api.supplybase.co.in. Do not include a trailing slash.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8080

# --- Google sign-in (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# The OAuth client id from Google Cloud Console:
#   APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> OAuth client ID
#   -> Web application
#   -> Authorised JavaScript origins: http://localhost:5173 (and your live
#      domain when you deploy)
#
# This MUST be the same value as GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID in backend/.env — the
# backend checks that a token was issued for this exact client id, and a
# mismatch means every Google sign-in is rejected.
#
# Leave blank and the Google button simply does not appear; email and password
# sign-in works either way.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# --- Partner portal (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# The address of the separate partners app (the partners/ folder), where
# professionals apply and sign in, for example https://partners.supplybase.co.in.
# No trailing slash.
#
# Leave blank until that app is deployed: the footer's "Partner Login" link is
# hidden and any old /partner link goes to the home page, so the website never
# points at something that is not there yet.
VITE_PARTNERS_URL=

# --- Google Maps location picker (optional) --------------------------------
# A browser key from Google Cloud Console with the "Maps JavaScript API" and
# "Places API (New)" enabled. RESTRICT it (Application restrictions ->
# Websites) to your domains, e.g. https://www.supplybase.co.in/* and
# http://localhost:5173/* — like every VITE_ value it is visible to anyone.
#
# Set it and the header location and the booking form offer the map picker
# (search, tap the map, or use the current location). Leave blank and the
# site keeps its city list and typed address.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
